From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:03:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] qt: draw a phone skin around the screen, with keys that
 light up and can be touched

A skin is a JSON layout next to two pictures: the phone, and its keys lit.
The layout gives where the screen goes and where each key is, with the
scan code it sends. skin-layout is used while the screen is taller than
wide, skin-layout-wide (when set) while it is wider.

The phone is drawn as big as the window allows and the screen fills the
place drawn for it. A key the device has down, from the keyboard, a pad
or a touch, is drawn lit: the window server now tells a key watcher
about every key it ships. A touch that starts on a drawn key presses
that key until the finger is lifted.
